/E (In conclusion, the analysis of the Casablanca-Settat provinces reveals disparities in health, education, and employment between urban and rural areas. Targeted policies are necessary to improve access to healthcare services, expand education in rural regions, and promote job creation. An integrated regional approach, balancing investments, is essential to reduce inequalities and improve the quality of life.)
